    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The source ranges over one-free-variable formulas F(x) of L_EA, for which arithmetic supplies a diagonal sentence. Lean ranges over arbitrary functions `Fm → Fm`: it neither requires F to arise from substituting a sentence code into a formula nor obtains the fixed point from a diagonal lemma. Def5 instead assumes the needed fixed point for the chosen F."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The single type Fm has no distinction between arithmetic sentences of L_PA, mentioned in the lead-in to Theorem 3, and sentences of the expanded language L_EA. The pointwise premise ranges over all of Fm, with no object-language arithmetic or quantifiers."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The scope of K in the pointwise premise and the existential conclusion both match Theorem 3. The target captures an abstract sufficient-conditions version of the theorem, but its conditions are not a rendering of theory inclusion itself."
